Somebody told me the class has to be `open` for Kora aspects. Is that the problem?

We migrated a Kora 1.x service to 2.0. The app starts fine but our Quartz thread pool size and shutdown settings are being ignored. application.conf has:

quartz {
  "org.quartz.threadPool.threadCount" = "30"
}
scheduling {
  waitForJobComplete = false
}

Why is nothing applied?

My long-running Quartz batch job in Kora 2.0 must stop cleanly on SIGTERM. Our 1.x service had this loop, and a colleague says Quartz never interrupts jobs so it is dead code:

for (var item : items) {
    if (Thread.currentThread().isInterrupted()) return;
    process(item);
}

Should I delete it? What happens on shutdown?
